organization: LEGO System A/S, Denmark
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1,comp.protocols.snmp,comp.dcom.net-management,comp.sys.dec


tom@finwds01.tu-graz.ac.at (Thomas Leitner) wrote:

>BTW: The management software is supposed to be PolyCenter Manager
>on Netview. What if I skip the DEC implementation of SNMP alltogether
>and go for, say, the UCD extensible SNMPD which is a freely available
>extensible SNMPD. 

>Will this make any difference from the management side (NetView) ?

I don't think so.

You will need the Common Agent if you want to run POLYCENTER on
Netview (PNV) on the Computer since it requires it.

But PNV doesn't care what kind of SNMP-Implentation runs on the Agent.
Basic PNV is just a SNMP management console.

Maybe you can get some special information via DECs SNMP agent
implementation (like disc usage, etc).

We are using the "Common Agent" here sine we run PNV on this machine.
But we don't use PNV to monitor our machines. Its solely purpose right
now is to monitor our IP and DECNet network.

Hope this helps.


