Good day,

     serviced a lot of PDP 8a/e/f/m in factory environment and in most 
cases the problem with the core memory is caused by
1.   metal dust built up in the ring (spray it out with a contact 
cleaner)
2.   corrosion on the modules contacts (use a pencil erasure to burnish 
them and then wipe them down with alcohol)
3.   backplane full of crap (this is always the fun one...tak it all 
apart, drop the backplane on the floor a few times (a couple of inches 
only) then liberally spray it out with contact cleaner.

typical symptoms 
- random hangs
- failure to load binary tape (but rim loader works just fine)


Brian V

good luck 




