Subject: routing problems & dns problems on Ultrix
Date: 1996/05/30
Message-ID: <4olbse$59i@missun.cus.cul.ca>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 157632649
organization: Canadian Utilites Limited, CU Services
keywords: dynamic routing
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


I am having problems on a server that worked just fine two days ago.

The Problem:
When the server first boots it is able to ping itself by name
and by IP address. It can also ping other hosts out on the Internet.
I can use nslookup interactively

Over the course of a few minutes of operation, dynamic entries 
start showing up in the routing tables. This did not happen
when we were on the Class B network. When some combination of
routes gets into the tables, the server cannot ping itself or
the default gateway. nslookup can only connect to localhost.
Flushing the routing tables and recreating the default route
makes it work for a while. (ie minutes)

What Has Changed:
1)
The network was originally class B.
It is now a collection of 64 contiguous super-netted class C networks.
It is also now using Cisco routers. (I don't control these)

2)
The netmask was 255.255.255.0
It is now 255.255.252.0
The broadcast was nnn.nnn.nnn.255
It is now mmm.mmm.mmm.255 with the top 3 octets matching the 
top three octets of the IP address. This is as it was before just
with changes appropriate to the new IP address.


3)
The default router is now mmm.mmm.128.254

4)
The server's IP address is now mmm.mmm.129.1
 (the 129 is not a typo, the 3rd octet is different from the default router)

5)
DNS tables were modified to reflect the change in the IP address
of the server and other systems that it is the name server for.

6) A single ifconfig command use to configure the network.
   ifconfig ln0 nnn.nnn.nnn.nnn netmask 255.255.255.0 broadcast nnn.nnn.nnn.255
   This does not work any more.
   Instead I have had to break it down to two commands or else the
   value I want for the netmask is ignored by Ultrix and stays at 255.255.255.0.

   ifconfig ln0 mmm.mmm.mmm.mmm broadcast nnn.nnn.nnn.255
   ifconfig ln0 netmask 255.255.255.0


Question:
Is there a way to configure the interface on the server to
ignore the dynamic routing information coming from the network
and just send to the default router?
Help would be greatly appreciated.

I have scanned through the FAQ but did not see anything about routing
problems of this nature.

Please reply to mallard@enr.gov.ab.ca


Thanks
Derek Mallard



