>problems of this nature.

The problem is that Ultrix doesn't know supernetting from a hole in the
head.  The TCP/IP code in Ultrix is truly ancient.  I would fix the
problem (there are other workarounds):

Kill routed and throw it as far away as possible!
Add a static route to mmm.mmm.128.0:
     route add mmm.mmm.128.0 mmm.mmm.129.1 0
Add a static default route:
     route add default mmm.mmm.128.254 1
You would probably need to add static routes to each of your class C nets.

