In article <4oidj7$jkj@sylvia.smith.edu>, cmeadows@smith.edu (Calvin J. Meadows) writes:
:
:Can someone tell me what would be required to cluster 2 DEC3000-600 systems?
:Both have the PMAZC-AA Dual Turbo channel controller. Each system has a BA350
:expander box connected to the Turbo Channel. 

   You'll need an Ethernet or FDDI connection, and you'll be able to
   configure these systems into a VMScluster.

   The KZTSA controller is the only TURBOchannel controller presently
   supported for dual-host SCSI clustering, and this configuration
   requires OpenVMS Alpha V6.2-1H2 or V6.2-1H3.  (These V6.2-derived
   releases post-date OpenVMS Alpha V7.0, and the hardware support
   added in these releases is not presently available in a V7-derived
   release.)

   With the KZTSA or any other SCSI-cluster-capable controller, one
   also needs an Ethernet or FDDI connection between the VMScluster
   member nodes.  (Much like the KFQSA adapter...)

  ------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
