[Howard Slomer]

> The system is a Decstation 5000/20, [...] passwords [...] forgotten

[Ilya]

> If the passwords are unknown, then you will have to reinstall the OS.

Actually, unless this is a very late version of Ultrix, it's possible
to boot passwordless to single user mode to change the password.  It's
been a while since I've used Ultrix on DECstations, so I don't recall
the sequence of actions and commands needed, but I'm sure someone can
supply these.

> I heard it can run some version of FreeBSD.

Nope.  It can run NetBSD, though.  NetBSD, like FreeBSD, is a 4.4BSD,
but whereas the FreeBSD team aims for maximum performance and hardware
option support on the Intel platform, the NetBSD project prioritizes
supporting many different hardware platforms.  The DEC MIPS platform
is just one of many -- I run NetBSD on Intel and VAX myself, and
Macintosh, Atari and Amiga are other well-known hardware bases for it.
Check out http://www.netbsd.org/ for more info.

-tih



