  The above statement is _not_ correct.  Ultrix (and many other
flavors of UNIX) can be brought to the single-user shell by
booting the system, watching for the message "Automatic reboot
in progress," and hitting CTRL-C.  Once in the single-user shell,
passwords may be changed.

