In article <4o01rc$4jp@sjx-ixn4.ix.netcom.com>, afish@ix.netcom.com(Andy Fish) writes:
|I would like to set up a DEC Alpha running VMS as a WWW server as well
|as use the X terminals on the system as a local and remote system
|browser.  The first question is - Are there any X Terminal Browsers
|that run under VMS?

I'm not clear on what you mean by an "X Terminal Browser".
If by "Browser" you mean a WEB browser, then, yes, there
are several Web browsers available for VMS.  

I use Mosaic 2.4, which is available from various sites.
If you have MultiNet TCP/IP installed on your system, then
it comes with the EMOSAIC browser built in.  A port of the
Netscape browser to VMS is rumored to be on the way ...

|The second question deals with having an application submit e-mail to
|the internet.  What programs are involved, where do you get them, or is
|there a syntax under MAIL> that will submit them automatically?

Ordinarily you would send Internet email from your VMS system by
having a TCP/IP package installed.  You have your choice
of UCX from Digital, MultiNet from Cisco, Pathway from
Attachmate, and TCPware from Process.  

I believe that each of these packages includes an Internet
mail system which interfaces into VMSMAIL.  With UCX or
MultiNet installed, you would sent Internet mail thus:

MAIL> SEND
To: SMTP%"user@hostname"

There are add-on mailers available - most prominently the
freeware MX package (from FTP.SPC.EDU and elsewhere) and 
PMDF from SALES@INNOSOFT.COM.

