We had a similar experience with these things. Interesting, because DEC told
us they hadn't seen this problem with anyone else, and ended up replacing our
tape drive (after weeks of complaining by us) and sending our old one to Engineering.

We bought five. One wouldn't work 7 times out of 8. One had lots of the same kinds
of errors, then suddenly started working fine. One sometimes failed, then suddenly
started working fine.

Anything that backed up okay was retrievable, though. We tested that.
And you're right about the TLZ6's; we have one that's been working for
quite some time, and never had any problems. All of our TLZ7's appear to 
be working fine, now, too. 

