The relevant part of the above DIR/FULL is the "Record format: 
Variable length" (shorthand: "RFM:VAR").  This means that the
each record is actually stored on disk with a 16-bit byte
count, then the record contents, then possibly a null byte to
pad the record out to a word boundary.

Use DUMP on this file to see what's REALLY in it.  One thing that
you'll find that their AIN'T no carriage return record separators.

