Kostas Kritsilas (kritsilas@plntree.synapse.net) wrote:
: Just picked up a VaxStation2000 from a surplus dealer. The system is
: booting up, showing VMS V5.3.1. However, it never completes the boot
: up process, indicating that SVA0 is losing sync, then showing that
: SVA0 is up, and repeating the cycle over and over again.

: I have tried to put a terminator on the BNC network connector ( switch
: on back to Position "A"), to no avail. Does anybody have any ideas on
: how to get this thing to come up without having a real network?

How about not starting the network?
Remove the call to SYS$STARTUP:STARTNET.COM from the SYSTARTUP_V5.COM.

You can bypass normal bootup by booting minimal (should be something
like >>> BOOT/R5:1 and then SYSBOOT> SET STARTUP_P1 "MIN"), so
SYSTARTUP_V5.COM will not be executed. Don't forget to reset
STARTUP_P1 to "" afterwards.

cu,
