From: Russell Vale <vale@vi.rl.ac.uk>
Subject: Success reading DECmate 5.25" floppies
Date: 1996/05/24
Message-ID: <4o4bnj$ko2@newton.cc.rl.ac.uk>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 156512073
content-type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
organization: CMF,RAL,UK
mime-version: 1.0
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec.micro,comp.sys.dec
x-mailer: Mozilla 1.1 (Windows; I; 16bit)


Hi,

Many thanks to all those who helped Brian Jones and myself with the 
problem of reading data from 5.25" floppy Decmate disks. Here is how I 
got it working.

When I tried running the software from a bootable 3.5" floppy disk the 
RAWREAD software would read OK from the DECmate floppy in drive B, but 
when it tried accessing the A drive to store its image copy of the disk 
it kept coming up with read errors which meant I couldn't store the disk 
image file. This was solved by booting from the hard disk and using the 
hard disk to store the image file. The DMPROCES software was then able to 
extract the documents from this image file.

In the documentation that comes with Kevin Handy's software it says that 
the CONFIG.SYS file has to have an entry device=raindos/d:1/f:0
This didn't work for me - error message was Bad or Missing RAINDOS. By 
changing the line to DEVICE=RAINDOS.SYS /D:1 this booted up OK and I was 
able to run the software successfully.

The documentation also says you need to have a file called RAINDISK.SYS 
on the bootable floppy - this should read RAINDOS.SYS

For those of you that need to find the RAINDOS software you can find it 
at the anonymous FTP site sunsite.unc.edu

under the directory
/pub/academic/computer-science/history/pdp-11/venix

in the file
raind112.zip

This is the configuration I found worked for me. It works on a Viglen 486 
with a 1.2 Mb 5.25" drive.

Thanks to the following people for helping with our query:

Kevin Handy
Chris Ketley
Bruce Maytum
georgee@decus.org.au
Dave Searle
Andy Wagliardo




