    The LA210 uses two switch packs labeled 'A' and 'B' on the rear of
    the unit to select communications features.  Use the following
    procedure to determine the current settings:

         o  Press "Off Line" to take the unit off line.
         o  Press "Self Test" to print the current settings.

    LA210 Switch Settings

    Restraint Mode
    A-1  Down selects restraint using BUSY line
         Up   selects restraint using SPDI/SPDS lines

    Modem Control
    A-2  Down   disables modem control signals

    Fault Response
    A-3  A-4
    Down Down   no action
    Up   Down   send break
    Down Up     disconnect (drop DTR)
    Up   Up     do no connect

    EOT
    A-5  Down   ignore EOT
         Up     enable disconnect

    XON/XOFF
    A-6  Up     enable XON/XOFF

    Error Processing
    A-7  Down   print substitute character
         Up     print as received

    Store Features
    A-8  moving the switch from down to up stores computer-selectable
         features in permanent memory

    Baud Rate
    --------------------------------
    B1   B2   B3   B4   B5
    --------------------------------
    Down Down Down Down Down    50
    Up   Down Down Down Down    75
    Down Up   Down Down Down   110
    Up   Up   Down Down Down   134.5
    Down Down Up   Down Down   150
    Up   Down Up   Down Down   200
    Down Up   Up   Down Down   300
    Up   Up   Up   Down Down   600
    Down Down Down Up   Down  1200
    Up   Down Down Up   Down  1800
    Down Up   Down Up   Down  2400
    Up   Up   Down Up   Down  4800
    Down Down Up   Up   Down  7200
    Up   Down Up   Up   Down  9600

    Split Baud Rates
    ----------------------------------
    B-1  B-2  B-3  B-4  B-5     T/R
    ----------------------------------
    Down Down Down Down Up     75/600
    Up   Down Down Down Up     75/1200
    Down Up   Down Down Up    150/600
    Up   Up   Down Down Up    150/1200
    Down Down Up   Down Up    300/2400
    Up   Down Up   Down Up    300/4800
    Down Up   Up   Down Up    600/2400
    Up   Up   Up   Down Up    600/4800

    Parity
    -----------------------------
    B-6  B-7   |   7-bits  8-bits
    -----------------------------
    Down Down  |   space   none
    Up   Down  |   mark    none
    Down Up    |   even    even
    Up   Up    |   odd     odd

    Data Bits
    B-8  Up   8-bit
         Down 7-bit

    Parallel Interface Switches
    Both Up   parallel interface turned OFF
    Both Down parallel interface turned ON

This information came from the LA210 Operator and 
Programmer Reference Guide (EK-LA210-RC).

