Hi

I recently purchased 4 TLZ07's in various configurations and 3 of them have
had to be replaced. They all exhibited the same fault, that is, they wrote
the data without complaint, but I couldn't read that data back reliably - 
the worst sort of senario!. I was using VMS Backup and Digital Unix's
Dump utilities.

The error pointed to a media problem (parity errors & positioning errors)
after testing with a multitude of new tapes from different manufacturers
and running cleaning tapes thru, I ended up having the drives replaced.
2 of the 3 replacements are now working fine. 1 of the replacements is
about to be replaced (yep, the same fault).

Has anyone else noticed problems with their TLZ07's? Are you sure your
backups are okay? If you don't use /VERIFY then I suggest you try to
list some of your tapes, just to be on the safe side.

I've been happy wih the TLZ06's, but I'm still to be convinced
that the 07's are anything other than expensive paperweights.

(and I don't want to hear from another person that I should have gone with
DLT drives instead!)

