I think you'r confusing Xinu and mt xinu. Xinu is Comer's operating system 
described by a book whose title escapes me at the moment (but a copy is
sitting on a bookshelf downstairs). I may recall incorrectly, but I don't
recall mt xinu running on PDP-11s.

Xinu is not a general-purpose operating system in the same sense as, say,
RT-11. It is a set of library routines linked with an application to provide
operating system services. The image it runs is static; you don't get a shell
from which you can launch applications which are not already built into the
system.

If I were me, I'd just leave it running MUMPS. MUMPS has always looked like
an interesting language, but I've never had the opportunity to play with it.
