Lonnie,

I own a DEC DSP3105 SCSI drive and have been very happy with it.  Have had it 
for more than 18mos now without any problems.  Here is some info that may help 
you...

DEC Installation Guide (covers DSP3000 series drives) p/n: EK-RH2CA-IG.A01
DEC Product Description Manual p/n: EK-RH27A-PD.A01
Perhaps you can request these directly from DEC now that you have part numbers?

Some specs from the Install Guide...
Unformatted Capacity:  1,372MB  (1 MB = 1,000,000 bytes)
Formatted Capacity:  1,600MB  (1 MB = 1,000,000 bytes)
Interface transfer rate:  Synch @ 10MB/s,  Asynch @ 5MB/s
Cache buffer size:  512KB
Track-to-track seek:  1.0mS
Average seek:  9.5mS
Maximum seek:  19mS
Rotational speed:  5,400rpm
Average latency:  5.6mS

Mean Time Between Failure:  250,000hrs
Power Requirements:  +5vdc +/- 5%  and  +12vdc +/- 5%
Max Current Consumption:  0.71A on +5  and  0.85A on +12  (13.7watts)
Acoustics (during seek, @ 1.0 meter):  40dBA

Jumpers, Front Set...
=========================== (pwa)
  o o o   o o o o o o
  o o o o o o o o o o
  1   5   9   13  17

Pin  Signal                            Pin  Signal
 1   ID (1) L                           2   Logic ground
 3   ID (2) L                           4   Logic ground
 5   ID (4) L                           6   Logic ground
 7   Fault LED Output L                 8   (key)
 9   Busy LED Output L                  10  Spindle Sync Reference L
 11  +5vdc Output (for LEDs)            12  (reserved)
 13  Motor Spin-up w/power on           14  Logic ground
 15  Power Fail Warning Input L         16  Logic ground
 17  (reserved)                         18  (reserved)
 19  Spindle Sync Reference L           20  Logic ground

- Place jumpers on pins 1-2, 3-4, 5-6 to set SCSI IDs.
- Place jumper on pins 13-14 to have drive motor spin-up on power-up.  If not 
jumpered, drive motor will only spin up when SCSI spin-up command received.
- Connect external "activity/busy" LED across pins 9-11


Jumpers, Underside of PWA Near Terminators...

                               A   C
                                o o
                                o o
                               B   D
  ==========  ==========  ==========
  1           1           1

- Install jumpers A-B and C-D so drive will supply TermPower to the SCSI bus 
and the termination resistors.


Hope this gives you enough info.  If you'd like several of the pages FAX'd to 
you, please send me an Email.

