Sounds like you may have the DSP3105D rather than the DSP3105S.  According to 
the install guide, the "D" model has an 8-bit differential SCSI interface 
while the "S" model has an 8-bit single-ended SCSI interface.  Placing a shunt 
on the single jumper near the SCSI connector will make the drive provide 
TERMPWR to the SCSI bus.  I can't find anything in the guide that mentions the 
jumper near the middle of the board.  Also the picture for the "D" model does 
**not** show any terminators near the SCSI connector.  Sounds even more like 
the drive you have.

