>Does anyone know what the jumper settings on this are?  Better
>yet, does anyone know what this drive is?

A DSP3105 is essentially an RZ26 if I remember right...

Jumpers are as follows:

Looking at front of unit, numbers are from left to right
(first three are SCSI ID, 7th is spinup on powerup/command)


SCSI ID	MSB		LSB
	2	1	0
0	Out	Out	Out
1	Out	Out	In
2	Out	In	Out
3	Out	In	Out
4	In	Out	Out
5	In	Out	In
6	In	In	Out
7	In	In	In

Jumper 13 and 14 (pair 7)
In	Spin-up on power-up.
Out	Spin-up on SCSI command.



