Nik Zapantis wrote:
> 
> I have an AS 200 4/100 system. I run both VMS and Windows NT.
> The system has 32MB of 70ns parity SIMMS.
> I would like to know if it is possible to use
> 1) non-parity SIMMS (together with the parity SIMMS already installed)
> 2) Use 60ns SIMMS (together with the 70ns already installed)

Hi Nik,

The AlphaStation 200 needs one parity bit for each longword. It works
with either 33- or 36-bit SIMMs (three bits are unsed on the 36-bit 
SIMMs).

If you try the 60ns SIMMs, it's probably best to keep them together in 
the same bank.

