Actually, is should run RT-11 just fine (RT will run on a memory
management
less LSI-11 (like an -03)) as well as RSX.  DEC sold all the rights on
the
PDP-11 software off recently.

It will run very old UNIXES.  Version 2 BSD (ran up to release 11 or
so).
A 11/73 even has split I/D so you can get the later versions that run
TCP/IP (the 23 and the non-split I/D machines ran out of segment
registers
to manage the overlays and data mapping required).  No, I have no idea
where
or how you could obtain either the license or the software to run UNIX
on
the beast.

Of course, it's purely an exercise in history, any PC from a 386 on will
have better performance (and support a more recent version of UNIX-like
OS's).

