In article <4nfauc$fap@newshub.atmnet.net>, jjo@triton.com (Jay Olson) writes:
:I have been lent a VAXstation 4000/60 for use on a project. I
:would like to use it with a serial console device, and no graphics
:display, mouse, and keyboard. Is that possible?...

  It's best if you acquire a monitor for the system -- running this box
  as a workstation is prefered, and is the (only) supported configuration.

  To run with a terminal as the system console, there exists an "S3" slide
  switch behind the front panel door on the system enclosure.  Slide it up.
  There is an MMJ connector on the back of the system -- see the OpenVMS
  Frequently Asked Questions for the MMJ pinout and available adapter part
  numbers -- that is used (if memory serves) as the printer port.  Plug the
  console terminal into this MMJ port.  (You will want to keep a keyboard
  plugged into the keyboard socket on the back of the system enclosure.)

  You should be off and running.

