  > Please tell me 
  > How to set up setting to spin up on when power on at same time? The
  > disk name is RZ28. 
  > And using windowsNT or Windows 95 

   According to some information I have here on the RZ28, there
   is a 20-pin 'options connector' socket on the drive, in which
   pins 13-14 should be jumpered to enable the 'spin on powerup'
   option.
   (Pins 1-2, 3-4, and 5-6 are the SCSI ID selection jumpers,
   where the least significant bit is pins 1-2 and is located
   nearest to the 'edge' of the drive on the 20-pin connector..
   
          -------------------------------------
          |                                   |
          |                                   |
          |         HDA assy.                 |
          |                                   |
          ------------------------------------
          | |2........20|                     |
          | |1........19|                     |
          | __________________________________|
          

