I've got an RZ25-E, and if it is similar to the RZ25-L, then SCSI 
termination is via Terminating Resisters. The manual states the 
following:

Three terminating resistors are also provided with the drive.
<snip a bunch of text that explains what termination means>
    
-----------------------NOTE--------------------------
When you install the terminating resistors, you must
maintain Pin 1 orientation.  Pin 1 on the terminating
resistor is marked with a dot.  Pin 1 on the drive is
located on the bottom of the drive next to the power
connector.  All three terminators must be installed
in-line behind the ribbon cable connector.
-----------------------------------------------------

It also mentions Terminator Power:
----------------------------------
Terminator Power is supplied by the drive.  Jumper block J6,
position 7 and 8, should be installed for Terminator Power.

And Parity Checking:
--------------------
Parity Checking is enabled.  Jumper block 6, position 5 should
be installed for Parity Checking enabled.

And Spin Up:
------------
The motor will SpinUp immediately when power is applied to the
drive.  Jumper block 6, position 2, should NOT be installed for
Spin Up on Power. (Install Jumper on position 2 to have SpinUp
on SCSI command rather than on PowerUp.)

And SCSI ID:
------------
Jumper block 5 (the 3 pin block), is for the SCSI ID setting:
    ID  Pin1 Pin2 Pin3
     0  Out Out Out
     1  Out Out In
     2  Out In  Out
     3  Out In  In
     4  In  Out Out
     5  In  Out In
     6  In  In  Out
     7  In  In  In
     
Hope this helps you out, and if you want/need any further info, 
please let me know.

-Stan




