                               RELEASE NOTES
                               -------------
             NBS Pascal Version 1.6iec  January 1986 for RT11

1.0  HISTORICAL NOTE

     The  first  version  of the NBS Pascal compiler used by the author was
version 1.6e.  This version had a great deal of  work  done  to  it  in  an
attempt  to  make  it  more  user  friendly,  eg not to crash when the user
responded with a carriage return to the argument line prompt, and  to  make
it work properly, eg fix up problems in the support library.

     In mid 1983 a new version of NBS Pascal was received.  This was an RSX
version  dated  21  October  1981  and   had   the   identification   1.6i.
Unfortunately,  the  code generator for this version was for a machine with
FPP, and the machine on which the much altered 1.6e version of  NBS  Pascal
was maintained only had FIS hardware.  After some initial investigation the
FIS code generator was transplanted into  the  1.6i  compiler.   The  whole
thing was then bootstrapped onto RT11 using the 1.6e compiler.

     The  work  since  that  time  has been spent fixing any bugs that have
appeared.  All unresolved problems documented  in  NBUGS  distributed  with
1.6i have been resolved in one way or another.

2.0  OPERATING SYSTEM SUPPORT

     For  historical  and  financial  reasons,  this compiler has only been
implemented under RT11.  It has been used successfully with  many  versions
RT11 and TSX+.  [...]

7.0  BUG (gulp) REPORTS

     Bug  reports  will  reluctantly  be accepted and, although there is no
guarantee of a bug fix, every  attempt  will  be  made  to  look  into  the
problem.   When sending a bug report, try to isolate the problem to a small
code fragment and incorporate that into a small program.  Send a listing of
that  small  program  so that the bug can be investigated.  Even better, if
you can fix the bug, send the bug fix along also.

