Who knows about the DEC audio mme library ?

We have a problem with recording data through the built-in audio
interface: when stopping the recording (waveInStop()), the driver
seems to keep some thousand samples in inits FIFO. When starting
recording again (waveInStart()), these samples are delivered back
before the new samples. IT IS NOT POSSIBLE TO GET RID OF THESE
extra samples; the workaround given in the release notes, to call
waveInReset() before waveInStart(), does not work.

We have tried out several combinations of waveInStop(), waveInReset(),
and queueing or not queueing buffers at the end of the recording,
but none could solve the problem.

Does anyone have an idea how to get rid of these extra samples
(aside from restarting the mmeserver) ? It occurs for V1.4 - V1.6.
Or does anyone know if the problem has been solved for the V2.0
drivers ?

Thanks in advance!

Frank



