Ann Haas wrote:
> 
> Does anyone have any information on the exact type of simms used
> in the XL 266?... Documentation suggests that they are 72-pin
> simms... I've tried installing 72-pin non-parity simms (from
> another PC). The machine recognized the ram, but when NT booted
> (as I recall) there was some sort of parity error (do i just
> need parity simms?)... Any info would be great as I'd like to
> avoid the markup on actual Digital upgrades.
> 
> Thanks
> Ann Haas,
> annhaas@creative.netHi Ann,

The Alpha XL 266 (and 233) use up to three banks of memory ( two 
72-pin SIMMs per bank). Longword parity is used (one parity bit 
for each 32 data bits). The system can use either 33- or 36-bit 
SIMMs.

A SIMM without parity is 32 bits, so you're going to need at 
least the 33rd bit to get the system going.

