>                     | Phone: +61 3 9596-2991    | 250 Bay St., Brighton,
> Standard disclaimer | Fax:   +61 3 9596-2960    | Vic., 3186, Australia
> --Hi Rob,

If IRQ5 is causing problems, you might try disabling the lpt1 (if 
it's not being used) to free up IRQ7. The command to do that is:

>>>isacfg -slot 0 -dev 4 -enadev 0 -mod

The you could adding your board with a command similar to:

>>>isacfg -mk -slot 1 -enadev 1 -etyp 3 -irq0 7 -handle TT

I think you also have to modify the file SYS$MANAGER:ISA_CONFIG.DAT
by adding a section similar to:
[TTA0]
      Name=TT
      Driver=sys$ysdriver
      IRQ=7
      Node=1
      Port=(address:length,address:length, ...)
The port line contains the address and address length for each 
port on the board and the status register (which should be listed first).
So, for a 4-port board, there should be five addresses entered.

