> Well, I managed to get another ST32550N with has a firmware level of
> 0014 instead of 0013 and this disk works now without a hitch.

  I believe the current ASA-I firmware (drive assemblies ending in -001)
is 0022 and the current ASA-II firmware (drive assemblies ending in -101)
is 0021. There were a bunch of changes between 0014 and these releases,
some of which do include fixes for bus errors during error recovery sit-
uations.

> Another thing I noticed which may be of some use for somebody:
> Badblock remapping is not turned on per default for Seagate disks
> (at least for the ST32550N's I got).
> 
> You can turn it on with "scu -f /dev/rrz8c change page error-recovery"
> and set ARRE as well as AWRE to on.

  You may want to see why you're getting read errors. Uncorrectable read
errors that don't go away when rewriting the sector's data are grounds for
replacing the drive.

