In case you haven't seen the announcements, the latest version of
Datatrieve does not require CDD/Repository or Rdb.  It can now store
all dictionary definitions as ordinary text files.  It will still
run with CDD/Repository if you have it, and can switch back and forth
as needed.

This doesn't solve the problem the original poster had about sharing
definitions with products other than Datatrieve, but it solves a lot
of problems for Datatrieve users who don't want or need CDD/Repository.

By the way, it starts up a lot faster without CDD/Repository.

