Firstly, I apologize for following up on one of my own messages - I've
been doing this more that I should lately.  Furthermore, I should have
read the fine manuals a bit more before posting my previous message
about adding a TU58 tape drive to my 11/73.

After some checking, I discovered that I have the documentation for
the DLV11-J, so I was able to examine the jumper settings on my M8043
and figure out that everything, except for some baud rates, was still
set for the factory default configuration.  The baud rate for port 0
is set to the default, 9,600 bps, so I guess (right or wrong) that
there's nothing that needs to be changed on this board.

It appears that the only thing which I'll need to do to get this to
work under RT-11 is to connect the cables, as "sh dev" displays
DD status as installed, with CSR=176500 and Vectors=300, 304. :-)

Getting this to work under TSX-Plus appears to be a bit more
complicated; actually, much more complicated, if I'm not mistaken
(which I very well could be).

When I did a "sh dev" under TSX+, no DD was listed; not surprising, as
I have no DD.TSX device handler.  I did find, in a older, V5.1,
distribution of TSX+, with patch files named DD500.SLP and DD600.SLP.
There are no DD*.SLP files in with my (partially complete?) 6.01
distribution; will I need them, or should the DD500 and DD501 .SLP
files be all that I'll need?

Am I going to need to define a line definition block to use the DL11
line No. 0?  Would it need to be something like (where ? denotes
unknown):

CLDEF  ?,300,176500
SPEED  S9600
FLAGS  ?
BUFSIZ ?
