Alan Frisbie wrote:
> 
> I am confused.
> 
>...
> What confuses me is the following:
> 
>    AlphaServer 1000                   AlphaServer 1000A
> 341 Transactions per SECOND        1150 Transactions per MINUTE
> 
> There is no explaination of why there is such a drastic
> difference between two almost identical machines, in articles
> run only three months apart.
>...
> Can someone tell me what is going on?   Also, exactly *what*
> is a transaction?The transaction numbers generally refer to TPC (Transaction
Processing Council) benchmarks.
The T/second numbers usually refer to the obsolete TPC-A benchmark,
which measured a very simple banking type transaction, whereas the
T/minute figures refer to the TPC-C benchmark, which is a more
complex order-entry transaction. The results are not really 
comparable in any way.
Even within TPC-C benchmarks, you can really only compare hardware 
if the same software is used, and the result is frequently
dominated by the disk systems rather than the CPU.

See the TPC home-page http://www.tpc.org/ for more info on the 
benchmarks and results.
The Ideas home page, http://www.ideasinternational.com/ also has
TPC and other benchmarks which might help you.
Good luck in interpretting all this information...
