and ask the question: Does anyone know if UDP checksums are commonly
done, or are they commonly disabled?  We've had problems in the past
with flaky bridge chips corrupting the packet when transferring UDP
packets from an ethernet chip (ethernet CRC passed) to main memory
(for IP stack processing), and the UDP checksum was not catching it
either because the sender was not calculating it, or the receiver was
ignoring it.

