a horse of a different color.

Under TSX+, the 11/73 has 25 serial ports configured (including the
console port), connecting to DB25 connectors.  The system also has an
additional four serial ports on an M8043 board, using the same type of
connectors that the TU58 drive uses.  This M8043 board isn't presently
being used for anything; I just stuck it in there to complete a grant
chain to get my RX02 drive to work.

Cabling wise, it's no problem for me to use this drive with either the
small plastic 14-pin connectors from the M8043 (as I've got one cable
with a 14pin connector on one end and a male DB25 on the other end,
and another similar cable, only with a female DB25 on one end - so I
figure that I can connect the two DB25 connectors and have a 14-pin to
14-pin cable from the two cables), or with one of the DB25 connectors
on the back of the system.

Software wise, am I going to need to run sysgen for TSX+ and RT-11?
Would there be any problem with using one of the additional ports on
the M8043 card with both TSX+ and RT-11?

Thanks very much in advance for any information that anyone can
provide about the above!  

