Every SCSI bus needs two terminators, one on each end, no more, no less. 
The computer doesn't know or care whether the device is internal or 
external. The only thing it MIGHT care about is what the SCSI ID was.

I would try changing the SCSI ID on your external drive to be the same 
as the dead internal one WAS.

