"Customer Update" on the AlphaServer 1000 and 1000A.
The first (1000) is in the November 1995 (Vol. 6, #11) issue
and the second (1000A) is in the February 1996 (Vol. 7, #2)
issue.

On the second page of each article is a list of features.
What confuses me is the following:

   AlphaServer 1000                   AlphaServer 1000A
        4/266                              4/266
   ================                   =================

341 Transactions per SECOND        1150 Transactions per MINUTE

There is no explaination of why there is such a drastic
difference between two almost identical machines, in articles
run only three months apart.

Similarly, in the April 1995 edition of DEC's "System Enhancement
Guide" is another set of conflicting data.   On page 7 are two
tables, "Cost of Operation Data for a Sampling of Systems" and
