Phil Wright (phil@wright.ftech.co.uk) wrote:

: Does anyone have an explanation for all of the cryptic monitor commands 
: (the >>> prompt at startup) other than the obvious help and b (boot) 
: commands? In particular do I need to reconfigure the system when I add or 
: remove cards? 

About the only ones you need to worry about are the 'SHOW' commands,
SHOW DEV, SHOW QBUS.  They will help you debug the hardware.  If
you don't have access to a running VAX system, you can also use
the CONFIG command to find out what CSR addresses to assign to
board.  But it's much easier to use /usr/field/shoaddrs than the
>>> CONFIG command.

: Is there any documentation for jumpers and LEDs on the Q-Bus cards?

Yes, but it's associated with the original document for each board.

: I have an RA70 drive, what do the "unit number accept" and "unit number 
: select" switches do, and is there a 'low level format' or other useful 
: software (running Ultrix) to check out the status of the drive other than 
: radisk?

Each drive on a controller has to have a unique ID.  Set one of them
to ID 0 and the second one to ID 1.  My MDM Customer Diagnostic TK50
doesn't include a low-level formatter for the RA70.  I understand it
only comes with the ENET version of the diagnostics, which only run
on VMS servers.  (There might be an Ultrix version, but I've never
laid eyes on it.)

Barry Kort



