On 8 May 1996, A.R. Duell wrote:

> gfrajkor@superior.carleton.ca (George Frajkor) writes:
> 
> I've changed the Newsgroups: line to more appropriate groups
> 
> > d) I have some cables left over from a PDP-11/34 to connect to RK06
> >drives.  They look exactly like the 11/23 - RL02 cables. They fit the
> >sockets and the connection snaps right in.  But are they the same??
> >The buses were different and I am afraid to try the older cables in
> >case they short something out.
> 
> The cables are different. The RK06/07 cables link all the pins except for 
> one (which is a +5V feed for a terminator), and the RL01/02 ones only 13 
> (?) pairs of pins. 
> 
> You can quite happily use RK06/07 cables to link up RL's, but not the 
> other way round.
> 
> 
> >     Nostalgia is an incurable disease.
> 
> Yes, thankfully :-)
> 
> >gfrajkor@ccs.carleton.ca
> >aa003@freenet.carleton.ca
> 
> --
> -tony
> ard12@eng.cam.ac.uk
> The gates in my computer are AND,OR and NOT, not Bill
> 
> 


So... that may be why my rk06 drives won't respond at all to the
controller.. I might be using rl cables.  I just assumed that dec wouldn't
be silly enough to make identical-looking cables with internal
differences.  Silly of me.  Are there any other reasons that the drives 
would act totally dead when referenced by the cpu?  They spin up ok, and 
find the home sector (at least the ready light lights..), but when I try 
to mount under rsx, it just sits.  Won't even crash because I guess it 
sees the controller...

Jake




