Kevin Girard (quon@idefix.seas.upenn.edu) wrote:
: 	o I need to update my firmware to at least v3.0 on my old SROM,
: 		then I can change to the new SROM, and boot up.

: I'm stuck on the fourth point here. I obtained media for firmware 3.0
: as well as Consolidated Software ECO Distribution, which I am told may
: be needed.

: My questions are, how do I install the new firmware? 

You need to (1) print out the installation instructions, which are on the
CD-ROM, and (2) boot the CD-ROM, which starts the firmware upgrade utility.
Step (1) is explained in the 10-page "Alpha Systems Firmware Update Version
3.5 Release Notes Overview" (AA-PW8YQ-TE, March 1996), which comes with the
CD-ROM, and step (2) is explained in the installation instructions.  THe
current firmware CD is version 3.5 (which installs console firmware 6.0
et al).  If you're going to do the installation, try to get the current
firmware version, as CD version 3.3 is minimum required for Unix 3.2C,
and 3.5 is required for Unix 4.0.

:I followed the DEC manual, and typed

: 	#/sbin/installupdate <device>

This is the procedure for an "update installation" of Unix.  You have to
do the firmware upgrade first, and, in any case, you'll find you have to
do a complete (full) installation to upgrade from Unix 1.2 to Unix 3.2C.

That's probably why you got the message you describe below.  You'll find it
easiest to install Unix 3.2C from scratch, unless you have a lot of customized
OS stuff.  Be sure to save all your files before doing a full install, as
they will all be destroyed.
