[Ari Suutari]

> Since I would love to have a VAX home I was wondering if it can be
> made to boot without graphics adapter using a vt220 terminal as a
> console ?

Yup.  You need the BCC08 cable, which is a 9-pin to 25-pin serial
cable that connects pins 8 and 9 on the 9-pin end.  This goes into the
printer port on the VS2000, and the 8-9 short tells the system to use
a serial console on that port instead of the graphics head.

Anyone have the exact BCC08 cable spec, though?  I'd like to make one
or two of them, and it would be nice to get it exactly right.

-tih



