A lot of the old minicomputers were, of course. Look at a PDP11 CPU - 
you'll see a lot of 74181 ALUs, small RAM chips for the registers, 
microcode proms, etc. The PERQ CPU board contains 5 74181 ALUs (it's a 20 
bit machine), 10 RAM chips for the 256 registers, a 2910 sequencer, 48 
RAM chips for the control store, and a lot of TTL and PROMs and PALs to 
link it all together.

