I guess ``Lige@txlutheran.edu'' has the firmware update CDROM but not
the instructions that go with it. No problem. The detailed descriptions
(including diagrams of the machines) are in a postscript file on
the CDROM! They are in the DOC subdirectory of the CDROM (which is
readable under VMS, UNIX and WinNT). The file you want is
    DEC3000_V64_FW_RELNOTES.PS (or .TXT)

I followed these instructions to upgrade both a 3000/400 and a 3000/300L.
Since the jumper is in a different place on the 3000/300, here is a diagram:

+-----------------------+
|   |                   |
|   |                   |
|   |                   |
|   |            +------|
|   |            |memory|
|   |   * %%%    +------|  * is the location of the jumper
|   +-+-----------------|  %%% is the SCSI connector
|fans |  hard  | floppy |
|     |  disk  |  disk  |
+-----+-----------------+
          front

Note: The drawing is not to scale :-) and the postscript is a hell of
a lot better than my ASCII art!

