Dave Schneider (dschneid@auc.trw.com) wrote:
: I'm looking for data on how fast I can push data over a network using
: TCP/IP.  I need to push data from one host to another that is divided
: into 7 logical streams.  I would like to make each stream a TCP/IP
: ...
:                       Total = 17.6 Mbyte/s
: ...
: Host A is known to be an SGI Challenge while Host B has not been
: selected yet.  Each host can have multiple network interface cards,
: ...
: The question is: Can this be done with today's technology (I think
: so).  I am looking for information so I can convince some others
: ... 
: Any information or references to data regarding this problem would
: be greatly appreciated (particularly actual test results). I will
: summarize the information that I receive and provide it to those
: that are interested.

There are snippets of information in the netperf database at
http://www.cup.hp.com/netperf/NetperfPage.html, but not a complete
package. For example, there is an SGI HiPPI number for a single TCP
stream of something over 700 Mbit/s, but it does not include CPU
utilization figures. There are CPU utilization figures for various HP
configurations, but none yet for interfaces faster than FDDI.

However, you might be able to glean some useful information.

rick jones



