the r10k can have 4 outstanding reads of 128-byte cache lines. it also
has four internal writeback buffers, and in the challenge r10k system, can
have two external writebacks in progress.

> Or is it that the R10K supports more outstanding transactions than
> the system it is currently shipping in (Challenge) allows from a single
> CPU?
> 
> I thought the Challenge bus supports 8 outstanding transactions?
> Do they each have to be from different CPUs?
> 

the challenge r10k product only supports a limited version of 2 
outstanding reads.  effectively, the 8 reads that can be outstanding 
on the challenge bus do have to be from different cpus.

