Libor wrote:
> 
> Using TCP/IP over HiPPI I've gotten rates of 20+ Mbyte/s (but not much over)
> This was between a cm5 to cm5, cm5 to sgi Challenge, and sgi to sgi. I hear
> that this is pretty common between most high performance machines using
> HiPPI. I believe that raw HiPPIs theoretical rate is 40 Mbyte/s in one
> direction, I'm not sure if this is for the PH or FP layer of HiPPI.

If that is true, the practical rate seems to be nearly double that rate :-).

I did measurements between a Cray C94 and a Cray Y-MP, connected via HIPPI and
achieved up to nearly 70 MB/s. My application had an available rate of approx.
50 MB/s (including all the overhead (even application-administration) of the
communication).

We would like to measure our application between a Cray and an SGI connected
via HIPPI, but we did not have the opportunity due to our lack of a HIPPI-SGI.

