I got home tonight to find Information Week had arrrived,
having a joint, two-page, innovative advertisement by Oracle and 
DEC.  Each company presents three of its officers making comments
about how wonderful the other company's products are.

Larry Ellison says, "Oracle is growing at a phenomenal rate.  We need
systems that can stay ahead of us, and our first AlphaServer tests
were truly incredibile.  We were floored.  It was a purchase decision
that made itself."

Robert Palmer says, "Oracle has an excellent record for seeing the
future clearly, so to have them running their most critical
applications on the AlphaServer platform is a tremendous
endorsement.  We're truly flattered."

This seems to be quite an interesting, and probably quite effective,
approach.  Someone should get a lot of credit for creativity.

